# Rules migrated → .cursor/rules/*.mdc

Cursor still loads this file on every turn, so it is intentionally kept thin.
The real rules are now scoped `.mdc` files under `.cursor/rules/`:

- `000-core.mdc`       — always-on protocol: knowledge-stack-first, think-before-coding,
                          goal-driven loops, surgical changes, report format
- `knowledge-stack.mdc`— full query-priority stack (ccc / graphify / wiki / decisions / interfaces / lessons)
- `ccc-search.mdc`     — ccc/cocoindex daemon operational guide (agent-requested)
- `prose-style.mdc`    — always-on prose principles: short, active, one-word-per-idea
- `session-lifecycle.mdc` — always-on rules for what stays in CLAUDE.md vs. sessions_summary/
- `embedded-c.mdc`     — STM32F4/FreeRTOS conventions + gotchas (auto-attaches on API/TASK/BSP/USER)

Custom commands: `.cursor/commands/` — type `/` in the Agent (session-start, session-end, diagnose, review, livewatch).

Workflow altitude — pick the right one:
- `/dispatcher`  — main session: what to build, which lane, flight-test queue (`.agent_contracts/ROADMAP.md`)
- `/wayfinder`   — one effort too big for a single spec; charts a map, resolves it one ticket per session
- `/uav-planner` — one task → `spec.md`. **Interactive** — grills you first. Never delegated to a subagent.
- `/uav-conductor` — implement → review → adjudicate, unattended, from an existing spec.

Skills (invoke by `name:` in frontmatter):
- Global: `~/.cursor/skills/` — goal-loop, decisions, next-decision, setup-help, git-worktree, anti-sleep
- Project: `.cursor/skills/` — dispatcher, planner, implement-spec, review-spec, parallel-implement, commit
- `.claude/skills/` — same skills, also available to Claude Code

Live firmware reads: `/livewatch` — read ANY firmware variable off the running drone by name
(read-only, no write path). ALWAYS `python -m ground_station.livewatch verify` first; a stale
`OBJ/JX_FLY.axf` returns plausible garbage, not an error. See `.cursor/rules/hardware-safety.mdc`.

Custom subagents: `.cursor/agents/` — `uav-conductor` (full pipeline orchestrator, Claude Opus 5
High), `uav-planner` (Claude Opus 5 High), `uav-implementer` (Cursor Grok 4.5 High Fast), and
`uav-reviewer` (GPT-5.6 Sol High, readonly). See `.cursor/agents/AGENTS.md` for the full index.

Safety hooks: `.cursor/hooks.json` runs two guards before every shell command:
1. `knowledge-gate.js` — nudges toward ccc before raw grep
2. `deny-dangerous.sh` (from `~/.agents/hooks/`) — blocks catastrophic commands (disk wipe, `git push --force`, `curl|sh`, fork bombs) before they run. See `~/.agents/hooks/dangerous-patterns.txt` to add patterns.
